{
  "$comment": "P0-43: the one scope map. ci.yml's `changes` job and the lead's gate.sh both read it through tools/ci-scope.mjs, so a lane runs for the same changed files in CI and in the local gate. A lane runs when a changed path starts with one of its `paths`, or with one of `shared` (the inputs every language verifies: the contract, the shared packages, the tool chain, the repository's own CI). On a push to main, and whenever the changed files cannot be read, every lane runs. `matrices` hold each matrix's two shapes: a pull request runs the floor and the latest, main runs the full set. Edit this file, never a path filter in a workflow.",
  "shared": [
    "conformance/",
    "packages/shared-",
    "packages/client-core/",
    "packages/brand/",
    "tools/",
    ".github/",
    "package.json",
    "pnpm-lock.yaml",
    "pnpm-workspace.yaml",
    "turbo.json",
    "tsconfig.base.json",
    ".npmrc"
  ],
